{
  "name": "film-stage",
  "version": "0.1.0",
  "private": true,
  "description": "three.js parts of a film's stage that any film shares: keyed camera with named eases and impact shake (camera); lighting rigs, IBL environments, probes, and area lights (lights); procedural skies, studio backdrops, clouds, stars, and sun/moon discs (sky); water, wet reflections, haze, physical materials, X-ray, beams, caustics, and flames (surfaces); atmospheric particle fields and ballistic emitters (particles); lookdev renderer, post-processing profiles, and screen effects (post); non-destructive outline and emissive highlights (highlight); flickering lamps (flicker); fades (fade); camera shot animations (animate); WebGL cut shaders (transitions); optical lens effects and beat accents (velocity); colour grading and TPDF dither (grade); titles and callouts (titles)",
  "type": "module",
  "exports": {
    "./openfilm": "./src/openfilm.ts",
